# Line endings.
#
# Development happens on Windows, where core.autocrlf rewrites checkouts
# to CRLF. Deployment happens on Ubuntu. A shell script that arrives with
# CRLF fails as "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" -- the shebang
# carries the carriage return -- and systemd and nginx are no happier
# with their own files. These must stay LF on disk, on both machines,
# because deploy/package.sh copies the working copy into the tarball.

*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf

# Keep diffs honest on everything else, and never touch binaries.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.webp          binary
*.ico           binary
*.woff2         binary
*.tar.gz        binary
*.zip           binary
